2026-11-07T06:43:44.7569140Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7602470Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7604010Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7605430Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7606000Z 
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7606780Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7607020Z 
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7607980Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7608360Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7609010Z 
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7609140Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7609390Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7609940Z 
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7610120Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:43:44.7610440Z   $ sh ./install-nix
